    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d175">

                <pb facs="0175" n="163" sameAs="frus:frus1943v04/pg163"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">868.00/1322a: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador to the Greek
                        Government in Exile</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">MacVeagh</hi>), <hi
                        rendition="#italic">at Cairo</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-12-23T21:00:00-04:00">December 23,
                            1943—9 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Greek [Series] 66. The British and Greek Ambassadors have both requested the
                    public support of this Government to the Greek Premier’s <pb facs="0176" n="164"
                        xml:id="pg164"/> radio appeal of December 21 for Greek unity. I understand
                    that a similar request has been made of the Soviet Government.</p>
                <p>You are authorized to deliver to the Prime Minister for use as he desires the
                    message contained in the Department’s next following telegram.<anchor n="69"
                        xml:id="d175-f1"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
